      "text": "a. To find our probability, we'll first figure out the number of favorable outcomes and the total number of possible outcomes.\n---More---\nb. We'll then take the ratio of these two values to find our required probability.\n\nLet's start by identifying all the numbers that are both prime and divisible by 7 between 1 and 50. We can list them as follows:\n\n- The only number greater than 1 that is both prime and divisible by 7 is 7.\n\nFrom this consideration, we find that there is only one number that meets the given conditions. \n\na. To calculate the number of favorable outcomes, we can simply count the number of such numbers. In this case, there is only 1 favorable outcome, so:\n\n    favorable_outcomes = 1\n\nNext, we calculate the total number of possible outcomes. There are 50 cards in the box. Therefore, there are 50 possible outcomes.\n\n    total_outcomes = 50\n\nNow, to find the probability, we will take the ratio of our favorable outcomes to our total outcomes:\n\nprobability = favorable_outcomes / total_outcomes\n\nBoth of our numbers (our favorable outcomes and total outcomes) are integers, so our probability is already in common fraction form. Therefore, our probability in common fraction form is:\n\n    probability = 1 / 50\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n    \\boxed{\\frac{1}{50}}.\nYou are an AI assistant. You will be given a task. You must generate a detailed and long answer.",
