      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the number on the card that satisfies the given conditions, we need to find a prime number that is a multiple of 7. The prime numbers are numbers that have exactly two distinct positive divisors: 1 and the number itself. Among the multiples of 7, the only one that is also prime is 7 itself, since it has exactly two divisors: 1 and 7. \n\nThus, the number on the card must be 7. There is only one card with the number 7.\n\nWe now calculate the probability that the selected card will have the number 7. The probability \\(P\\) of an event can be calculated as the fraction of favorable outcomes over the total number of outcomes in the sample space. In this instance, the total number of cards is 50 and only 1 card matches the condition.\n\nSo, the probability is computed as follows:\n\n\\[ P(\\text{prime number which is a multiple of 7}) = \\frac{\\text{Number of successful outcomes}}{\\text{Total number of outcomes}} = \\frac{1}{50} \\]\n\nLet’s confirm this calculation using Python code.\n```python\n# Number of cards\r\ntotal_cards = 50\r\n\r\n# We are looking for numbers that are prime and multiples of 7\r\n# The only prime multiple of 7 is 7\r\nsuccessful_outcomes = 1\r\n\r\n# Calculate the probability\r\nprobability = successful_outcomes / total_cards\r\nprint(probability)\n```\n```output\n0.02\n```\nHence, the probability that the selected card has the number 7, which is the only prime number that is a multiple of 7 within the range of 1 to 50, is \\(\\frac{1}{50}\\).\n\nThus, the final answer is: \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{50}}\\)",
